## 2. What SipSync Does (Feature List)

### 2.1 Smart Water Reminders
- Users set a custom reminder interval (e.g., every 15 minutes, every 1 hour).
- The extension fires a reminder at the set interval using Chrome's `alarms` API.
- Users can **Start**, **Save** (update interval), or **Stop** reminders at any time.

### 2.2 Dual Notification System
Users choose how they receive reminders in Settings:
- **OS Notification** — Native operating system notification with "I drank Xml" and "Ignore" action buttons (X = user's configured glass size).
- **Pop-up Reminder** — A dedicated browser pop-up window with a motivational quote, "I drank Xml" and "Ignore" buttons.
- Users can enable **one or both** simultaneously.
- Each notification includes two actions: **"I drank Xml"** (logs glass size intake) and **"Ignore"** (dismisses).
- **Anti-Reopen Protection:** Reminder popups validate an `activeReminderId` token on mount. If the token is already consumed (e.g., user presses `Cmd+Shift+T` to reopen a closed tab), the popup auto-closes immediately.

### 2.3 Intelligent Notification Management
- **Single-instance guarantee:** Only one reminder notification exists at a time. Before creating a new notification, any existing one (OS or popup) is forcefully dismissed.
- **Cross-dismissal:** Clicking on one notification type automatically closes the other (e.g., clicking "Drink" on the OS notification closes the popup window, and vice versa).
- **No notification bursts:** If the laptop was asleep or Chrome was closed, SipSync does NOT spam the user with all missed reminders. Only the latest single notification is shown.

### 2.4 Daily Water Intake Tracker
- Visual progress circle with animated water wave fill effect.
- Shows current intake (e.g., "1200ml") and percentage.
- Resets automatically every day at midnight.
- Users set a customizable daily goal (default: 2000ml, max: 6000ml).
- A "Drink a glass" quick-action button on the main screen (uses the user's configured glass size).
- **Intake Cap:** Total daily intake is hard-capped at 6000ml across all entry points (main popup, reminder popup, OS notification).
- **Reminder timer reset:** Clicking "Drink" from the main extension popup resets the reminder timer. Clicking from OS notifications or the reminder popup does **not** reset the timer — they continue on their regular schedule.
- **Interval blur validation:** If the user leaves the reminder interval input empty or invalid, it automatically snaps back to 45 minutes on blur.

### 2.5 Goal Completion Celebration
- When the user reaches their daily goal, SipSync celebrates!
- **If the extension popup is open:** Confetti animation fires directly inside the popup.
- **If triggered from a notification:** A separate celebration popup opens with confetti, a congratulatory message, and a special sound effect.
- **OS celebration notification:** Shows "🎉 Goal Complete!" native notification.
- Celebration notifications also follow the single-instance pattern (cleared before new reminders).

### 2.6 Sound Effects
- Customizable from Settings: toggle sound on/off.
- Reminder sound plays when a pop-up reminder appears.
- Special celebration sound plays when the daily goal is completed.

### 2.7 Settings Page
- **Reminder delivery:** Toggle OS notifications and/or pop-up reminders.
- **Sound:** Toggle sound effects on/off.
- **Glass Size:** Configurable glass size (default: 200ml, max: 1000ml). Displayed as a single-row setting with a chip-styled "ml" unit badge. The "Drink" buttons across the extension use this value.
- Footer pinned to bottom: "Built with ❤️ to help you stay hydrated and focus on what matters."
- Footer links: User Guide and Privacy Policy.

### 2.8 Statistics / Hydration Calendar Page
- Accessible via a chart icon button on the main homepage (beside the settings gear).
- **Monthly Calendar View:** Displays a full month grid with day numbers.
- **Medal System:** Each past day can earn a medal based on hydration goal completion:
  - 🥇 **Gold** — Reached ≥100% of daily target.
  - 🥈 **Silver** — Reached ≥75% of daily target.
  - 🥉 **Bronze** — Reached ≥50% of daily target.
- **Color-coded cells:** Days with medals get distinct background/border colors (amber for gold, gray for silver, warm orange for bronze).
- **Medal display:** Medals appear side-by-side next to the day number within each cell.
- **Month Navigation:** Previous/Next buttons to browse historical months.
- **All-Time Medal Totals:** Summary card showing lifetime gold, silver, and bronze counts. Unearned medals appear grayed out.
- **History-only data:** Medals are only shown for completed past days (stored at daily reset). Today's in-progress data is not displayed to avoid fluctuating medal states.
- **Consistent styling:** Uses the same background image as the homepage and settings page.

